comments:
@dummdidumm What is the difference between:
```css
	:global [data-blue] {
		.box {
			background: blue;
			animation: scale-ani 2s infinite;
	 }
	}
```
```css
	:global {
		[data-blue] .box {
			background: blue;
			animation: scale-ani 2s infinite;
	 }
	}
```
Why does first one works and second does not? They look identical from specificity point of view, only syntax differs. Nesting supposed to be only syntax sugar.

review_comments:
```suggestion
	e(node, "css_global_block_invalid_placement", "A `:global {...}` block can only appear at the end of a selector sequence (did you mean to use `:global(...)` instead?)");
```
